# Analyst Notes

File creation telemetry is an important component of endpoint monitoring. Threat actors commonly create payloads, scripts, scheduled task files, persistence mechanisms, and temporary artifacts during an intrusion.

Although file creation is a normal operating system activity, correlating these events with PowerShell execution, Command Prompt activity, Certutil usage, or administrative logons significantly improves detection fidelity and helps identify malicious behavior more effectively.
